# Content-Security-Policy is set PER-PAGE below, never on /*, on purpose:
# Cloudflare Pages JOINS (does not override) same-named headers across every matching rule,
# so a CSP on /* would stack with a page's CSP and the browser would enforce the INTERSECTION,
# which silently strips the swap page's 'wasm-unsafe-eval'/worker-src and breaks the Monero
# engine. Pages also 308-redirects /x.html -> the clean /x, so each page is listed on BOTH
# forms; a page left unlisted would land on the clean URL with NO CSP at all.
# Rule of thumb: strict CSP everywhere; permissive ONLY on the swap app + the Monero worker.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# STRICT CSP: every page except the swap app (listed on clean + .html URL forms)
