# PERMISSIVE CSP: the swap app (both URL forms) runs the tXMR->tBTC Monero engine (WASM +
#    Web Worker), which needs 'wasm-unsafe-eval' + 'unsafe-eval' + worker-src + the Monero node
#    origins in connect-src. The worker at /vendor/monero.worker.js runs WASM compile + node RPC
#    under its OWN response CSP, so it needs its own identical rule. default-src is 'self' (not
#    'none') here so the engine's same-origin module/worker loads (e.g. /vendor/swap-core) that
#    fall through to the default directive aren't blocked; script/connect/worker are still locked.
#    Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp + the /* Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
#    make the page cross-origin ISOLATED, which monero-ts needs for SharedArrayBuffer (its wasm
#    wallet is threaded). Safe because every cross-origin endpoint (api/relay/nodes/mempool/faucet)
#    sends Access-Control-Allow-Origin, so CORS resources still load under require-corp.
/swap
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'unsafe-eval' blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://api.testnetswap.com wss://relay.testnetswap.com https://relay.testnetswap.com https://testnetscan.com https://mempool.space https://xmr-testnet-node.librenode.com https://xmr-stagenet-node.librenode.com https://cypherfaucet.com; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
